# Create variables for three fictional customers, each with:

# tenure_months (an int)
# monthly_charges (a float)
# Name them clearly, e.g. customer1_tenure, customer1_charges, etc. (or use three small dictionaries if you completed that pattern in class).

# Create variables for three fictional customers

# Customer 1
customer1_tenure = 12
customer1_charges = 49.99

# Customer 2
customer2_tenure = 24
customer2_charges = 79.50

# Customer 3
customer3_tenure = 6
customer3_charges = 35.75

# Print customer details
print("Customer 1:", customer1_tenure, "months,", customer1_charges, "monthly charges")
print("Customer 2:", customer2_tenure, "months,", customer2_charges, "monthly charges")
print("Customer 3:", customer3_tenure, "months,", customer3_charges, "monthly charges")

# For each customer, compute and print whether they are a "high value, long-term" customer, defined as:

# tenure_months > 12   AND   monthly_charges > 70
# Print a clear, labeled result for each customer (e.g. "Customer 1 is high value & long-term: True").

# Check whether each customer is high value and long-term

customer1_status = customer1_tenure > 12 and customer1_charges > 70
customer2_status = customer2_tenure > 12 and customer2_charges > 70
customer3_status = customer3_tenure > 12 and customer3_charges > 70

# Print labeled results
print("Customer 1 is high value & long-term:", customer1_status)
print("Customer 2 is high value & long-term:", customer2_status)
print("Customer 3 is high value & long-term:", customer3_status)

# Pick one customer's monthly_charges and cast it to int.

# Print the original float value.
# Print the casted int value.
# In a comment, explain what value was lost and why (hint: int() truncates, it does not round).

# Pick Customer 1's monthly charges
original_charges = customer1_charges

# Cast float to int
casted_charges = int(original_charges)

# Print both values
print("Original float value:", original_charges)
print("Casted int value:", casted_charges)

# The decimal part (.99) was lost because int() truncates the value
# instead of rounding it to the nearest whole number.